--- !u!114 &1753929911
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1753929908}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 8d5be57ef61e14ff39321ed63a581266, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: AudioFeatureLab::AudioFeatureLab.DemoOverlay
  title: Mixer groups and snapshots
  body: 'Four looping sources feed four groups under Master: Music, Ambience, Sfx,
    and Voice. Open Window > Audio > Audio Mixer and select DemoMixer to see them.


    Keys
    1 through 9 crossfade snapshot A into snapshot B. 1 is entirely A, 9 is entirely
    B, 5 is even.

    Y cycles snapshot A. U cycles snapshot B. The set is Neutral,
    DialogueFocus, Underwater, and Outdoor.

    Underwater lowers music and effects
    and closes a low-pass on Master. DialogueFocus ducks music, ambience, and effects
    so the voice group leads.


    Z X C V B select Master, Music, Ambience, Sfx,
    and Voice.

    Up and Down nudge that exposed volume by 2 dB. SetFloat takes
    the parameter away from snapshots.

    Backspace calls ClearFloat on every exposed
    parameter and returns control to the snapshots.


    Select Snapshot Crossfader.
    blend, weightA, and weightB are the live mix.


    M menu. P pauses every voice
    (AudioListener.pause). [ and ] change AudioListener.volume.

    Click the Game
    view so the editor does not take the keys.'
  scroll: {x: 0, y: 0}
  width: 520
